course: dictionary
lesson: 2497
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The sadness after a death is called grief.» Here death means the end of a life, because grief is the sadness people feel when someone has died.
explain: «I was bored to death during the long wait.» Nobody actually died. Bored to death is an exaggeration, a way of saying something was extremely boring. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I take the word literally? If it does not, the writer is probably exaggerating.
explain: Some sentences are about numbers, like «most home fire deaths happen in homes without a working alarm.» Here deaths means cases of people dying, and most tells you it is a count. Check your meaning by swapping in your own words, such as "the number of people who died", and see whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Death means the end of life: a person, animal or plant dies and stops living for ever.
fact: «Deaths» can mean the number of cases of someone dying, as in «There were no deaths in the accident.»
fact: Death is part of the life cycle: all living things are born, grow, may reproduce and die.
fact: Phrases like «scared to death» and «bored to death» exaggerate a feeling; they do not mean that anyone has died.
fact: Grief is the sadness felt after a death, and it helps to talk about it with someone you trust.
exercise: «The sadness after a death is called grief.» In this sentence, what does death mean? | A loud noise in the night | *The end of life, when a person stops living | A kind of sad music | A very long holiday
exercise: «I was scared to death of the dark.» What does scared to death mean here? | *Extremely scared, a way of saying very scared | Lost in the dark for ever | Asleep and dreaming
exercise: «There were no deaths in the accident.» What does deaths mean? | Happy days | Rules about safety | Slow walks | *Cases of people dying
test: Lily says «bored to death» means she really died of boredom. Is she right? | Yes, boredom can kill people | No, it means very happy | Yes, it is a medical word | *No, it is an exaggeration meaning very bored
test: Which sentence uses death as an exaggeration? | *I was bored to death in the car. | Death means the body has stopped working for ever. | The sadness after a death is called grief. | Smoke alarms give families time to escape.
exam: Does «most home fire deaths happen in homes without a working alarm» talk about a number or a feeling? | A feeling of sadness | A colour | A type of weather | *A number of cases, shown by the word most
